The Kore Dashboard aims to be a central hub for managing and interacting with the Kore agentic framework. It should cater to various user roles, from developers building complex agent pipelines to business users monitoring their performance.

Here's a detailed list of key features, categorized for clarity:

---

## Kore Dashboard: Key Features

### I. Core Agent Management & Development

This section focuses on the creation, configuration, and structural management of agents and pipelines.

*   **Agent Definition & Creation:**
    *   **Agent Definition Canvas (Visual Editor):**
        *   Drag-and-drop interface for composing agents from pre-built components (tools, LLMs, memory, planners, etc.).
        *   Visual representation of agent flow, decision points, and tool usage.
        *   Ability to define agent roles, goals, and communication protocols.
        *   Support for nested agents and sub-agents.
    *   **YAML/JSON Editor (Code View):**
        *   Direct editing of agent definitions for advanced users.
        *   Syntax highlighting, auto-completion, and schema validation.
        *   Version control integration (Git-like history) for agent definitions.
    *   **Pre-built Agent Templates:**
        *   Gallery of common agent types (e.g., summarizer, data analyst, customer support bot) that users can customize.
    *   **Tool Management:**
        *   Repository of available tools (built-in, custom, third-party integrations).
        *   Tool creation interface (defining inputs, outputs, description, API endpoints).
        *   Tool versioning and dependency management.
*   **Pipeline Assembly (Agent Orchestration):**
    *   **Pipeline Builder (Visual Graph Editor):**
        *   Connect multiple agents to form complex workflows and pipelines.
        *   Define data flow, triggers, and conditional logic between agents.
        *   Visualize the entire agent network and its dependencies.
    *   **Pipeline Templates:**
        *   Predefined pipeline structures for common use cases (e.g., RAG pipeline, multi-step data processing).
    *   **Input/Output Mapping:**
        *   Clearly define inputs required for a pipeline and expected outputs.
        *   Data transformation capabilities between agent steps.
*   **Version Control & Deployment:**
    *   **Agent/Pipeline Versioning:**
        *   Automatic versioning of agent and pipeline definitions.
        *   Ability to revert to previous versions.
    *   **Deployment Management:**
        *   One-click deployment of agents/pipelines to different environments (dev, staging, production).
        *   Configuration of deployment parameters (resource allocation, scaling).
        *   Rollback functionality for deployments.
*   **Component Library:**
    *   **LLM Integration Management:**
        *   Configure and switch between different LLM providers (OpenAI, Anthropic, custom models).
        *   Manage API keys, model parameters (temperature, top_p).
    *   **Memory Management:**
        *   Define and configure different memory types (short-term, long-term, vector stores).
        *   Associate memory instances with specific agents or pipelines.
    *   **Planning & Reasoning Components:**
        *   Select and configure different planning algorithms (e.g., CoT, Tree of Thoughts) for agents.
    *   **Tool/Skill Repository:**
        *   Browse, add, and manage reusable tools and skills for agents.

### II. Execution & Interaction

This section focuses on running agents/pipelines and interacting with them.

*   **Agent Execution Interface:**
    *   **Manual Triggering:**
        *   Ability to manually submit inputs to agents/pipelines and observe their execution.
        *   Real-time display of agent's thought process, tool calls, and outputs.
    *   **Scheduled Execution:**
        *   Set up recurring schedules for agent/pipeline runs (cron-jobs).
        *   Define triggers based on external events (e.g., new file in S3, webhook).
    *   **API Endpoint Generation:**
        *   Automatically generate REST API endpoints for deployed agents/pipelines, enabling external integration.
        *   API documentation (Swagger/OpenAPI).
*   **Interactive Chat/Testing Environment:**
    *   **Agent Sandbox:** Run agents in an isolated environment for testing and debugging.
    *   **Conversational Interface:** Chat directly with an agent to test its responses and behavior.
    *   **Input Parameter Configuration:** Provide various input parameters to test agent behavior under different conditions.
    *   **Result Visualization:** Display agent outputs in a structured and easy-to-understand format (text, tables, charts).

### III. Monitoring & Observability

This section covers the tracking, analysis, and debugging of agent performance and behavior.

*   **Execution Logs & Tracing:**
    *   **Detailed Run History:** View a complete history of all agent/pipeline executions.
    *   **Step-by-Step Trace:**
        *   Visualize the exact sequence of actions, tool calls, and LLM interactions taken by an agent during a run.
        *   Display LLM prompts, completions, and token usage for each step.
        *   Highlight decision points and reasoning paths.
    *   **Error Reporting:** Centralized logging and display of execution errors.
    *   **Contextual Information:** Access the full context (memory, state) of the agent at any point during execution.
*   **Performance Metrics:**
    *   **Latency:** Average execution time per agent/pipeline.
    *   **Throughput:** Number of successful executions per unit of time.
    *   **Cost Tracking:** Token usage, API calls, and estimated cost per run.
    *   **Success Rate:** Percentage of runs completed without errors.
    *   **Agent-Specific Metrics:** Custom metrics relevant to the agent's task (e.g., accuracy for a classification agent).
*   **Alerting & Notifications:**
    *   **Customizable Alerts:** Set up alerts for failed runs, high latency, exceeding cost thresholds, or specific agent behaviors.
    *   **Notification Channels:** Integrate with email, Slack, PagerDuty, etc.
*   **Resource Utilization:**
    *   Monitor CPU, memory, and network usage for deployed agents.
    *   Identify potential bottlenecks or resource constraints.
*   **User Feedback & Evaluation:**
    *   Mechanism for users (especially business users) to provide feedback on agent outputs.
    *   Rating system for agent performance (e.g., "helpful," "not helpful").
    *   Ability to flag incorrect or undesirable agent behavior.

### IV. Debugging & Troubleshooting

This section provides tools to diagnose and fix issues within agents and pipelines.

*   **Interactive Debugger:**
    *   **Breakpoints:** Set breakpoints at specific steps in an agent's or pipeline's execution.
    *   **Variable Inspection:** Inspect the state of agents, memory, and tool outputs at breakpoints.
    *   **Step-Through Execution:** Step through agent logic one step at a time.
    *   **Rewind/Replay:** Replay problematic execution paths to reproduce issues.
*   **Error Analysis:**
    *   Categorization of errors (e.g., LLM hallucinations, tool failures, logic errors).
    *   Recommended actions or potential causes for common errors.
*   **Log Search & Filtering:**
    *   Advanced search capabilities for execution logs (by agent, time, status, keywords).
    *   Filtering by error type, duration, specific agents, etc.

### V. Security & Access Control

This section ensures the dashboard and agents are secure and accessible to appropriate users.

*   **Role-Based Access Control (RBAC):**
    *   Define roles (e.g., Admin, Developer, Analyst, Viewer).
    *   Granular permissions for creating, editing, deploying, and viewing agents/pipelines.
*   **User Management:**
    *   Add, remove, and manage users.
    *   Integrate with existing identity providers (e.g., SSO via Okta, Azure AD).
*   **API Key Management:**
    *   Secure storage and rotation of API keys for LLMs and external tools.
    *   Audit logs for API key usage.
*   **Audit Trails:**
    *   Track all significant actions performed on the dashboard (e.g., agent changes, deployments, user logins).

### VI. Collaboration & Sharing

This section facilitates teamwork and knowledge sharing.

*   **Workspace Management:**
    *   Organize agents and pipelines into projects or teams.
    *   Shared workspaces for collaborative development.
*   **Commenting & Annotations:**
    *   Ability to add comments to agent definitions, pipeline steps, or run logs.
*   **Export/Import Functionality:**
    *   Export agent/pipeline definitions (YAML/JSON) for sharing or backup.
    *   Import definitions from external sources.

### VII. Integration & Extensibility

This section addresses how the dashboard interacts with other tools.

*   **API Access:**
    *   Comprehensive API for programmatically interacting with the Kore framework from external applications.
*   **Webhook Integration:**
    *   Send notifications to external systems upon specific events (e.g., agent completion, error).
*   **Source Control Integration:**
    *   Connect to Git repositories (GitHub, GitLab, Bitbucket) for storing and versioning agent definitions.
    *   CI/CD pipeline integration for automated testing and deployment.
*   **Monitoring & Logging Integrations:**
    *   Export logs and metrics to external platforms (e.g., Prometheus, Grafana, ELK Stack, Datadog).
*   **Observability Integrations:**
    *   Connect with OpenTelemetry or other tracing systems for distributed tracing.

---

### User Roles & Feature Emphasis:

*   **Developers:**
    *   Heavy use of Agent Definition Canvas, YAML Editor, Pipeline Builder.
    *   Interactive Debugger, detailed Execution Logs & Tracing.
    *   Version Control, Tool Management.
*   **Operations (Ops):**
    *   Deployment Management, Performance Metrics, Alerting & Notifications.
    *   Resource Utilization, Audit Trails.
    *   Log Search & Filtering.
*   **Business Users:**
    *   High-level Performance Metrics (dashboard views).
    *   User Feedback & Evaluation.
    *   Pre-built Agent Templates, easy access to Agent Execution Interface (for interaction).
    *   Focus on clear status updates and business-relevant outcomes.

This comprehensive list ensures that the Kore Dashboard is a powerful, user-friendly, and indispensable tool for anyone working with the Kore agentic framework.
